<p><strong>LOG-001</strong>: “Hello from the Occator Crater. This is Dr. ██████, alongside my fellow researcher Dr. ███ █████. Communication Systems are functional, and we have successfully connected to Station Tau’s primary server. Our mission is the successful extraction of SCP-XXXX. I will also be reporting on a weekly basis the results of our findings.”</p>
<p><strong>LOG-002:</strong> “Day 7. Quantities of the fluid seem to get ejected from the chasm out into space continuously. It hasn’t ever stopped since we landed. However, the amount of fluid that gets ejected seems to rise and fall, at least according to our scanning systems. There are currently no correlations involving the increase or decrease in fluid ejection. I will state our findings in our next report.“</p>
<p><strong>LOG-003:</strong> Day 14. Me and Dr. ███ █████ have been trying to find any correlations involving the quantity of fluid that gets ejected, to no avail. We’ve tried finding if the presence of Station Tau in orbit changes the ejection level, no connection there. We’ve tried finding if the presence of the Sun changes the ejection level, no connection there. We’ve tried if our presence in Occator Alpha changes the ejection level, no connection there. (We only left Occator-Alpha for two hours, and our life signs are of no concern.) Daily operations mainly consist of me researching the ejection of SCP-XXXX, and Dr. ███ █████ researching methods of extraction.”</p>
<p><strong>LOG-004:</strong> Day 22. For some reason, when I tried to upload this log yesterday, all of Station Tau’s communication systems were offline. We are mainly focusing on physical methods to extract SCP-XXXX, but that idea is quite ambitious, considering the fact that we are █ kilometers away from the ejection chasm. However, we are making progress as the days go by, and I am fairly certain that we are closing in on an idea. Another interesting thing that happened two days ago was that while I was walking down the hallway, I passed by another version of myself. He bares no resemblance to Dr. ███ █████, and fully bares resemblance to me. That might be another thing to research in Station Tau. This might be a coincidence, or a lucid dream, but it is something to note.</p>
<p><strong>Log-005:</strong> Day 29. Me and Dr. ███ █████ have successfully found a method to extract SCP-XXXX from the ejection chasm. We are planning to build a linear transportation system up to the safe distance of the ejection site, and use a vacuum-like technology to extract SCP-XXXX. Afterward, it will flow through our transportation system, and into our laboratory. In order to prevent SCP-XXXX’s high heat levels from becoming a burden on our research, we have designed a system that will cool anything flowing through the transportation system to approximately absolute zero. That way, we’ll be safe, and so will SCP-XXXX. We have requested a few caches of building material and extra personnel to assist us in construction. On another note, the doppelganger of myself appeared a few times in the past seven days. It doesn’t seem to talk to me, but instead mumbles to itself. I will make a report on what it is trying to say if I find out.</p>
<p><strong>LOG-006:</strong> Day 36. Station Tau has greenlit our construction plans, and sent down all of our required materials and labor. They left a message simply stating to keep within the minimum safe distance, and to not construct the vacuum system until their Innovations Laboratory can design a more effective method of extraction. They have also given us permission to cease log uploads until construction is finished. Before I go radio-silent, I want to say that my doppelganger was saying some cryptic messages to itself. For example, it said that “Life is corruption, and I am the purification.” and that “The rising flood matters not in the scale of the universe.” I don’t understand what deeper meaning that had, but I do have a theory. It is entirely possible that ‘the rising flood’ is the ejection of SCP-XXXX, and that this clone is a manifestation of SCP-XXXX’s desires. Perhaps the philosophy majors up in Station Tau can figure that one out. Other than that, construction of the machine will begin posthaste, and I will return when it is complete.</p>
<p><strong>LOG-007:</strong> Day 246. Reporting back to Station Tau, because the construction of the machine has been completed. The Innovations Laboratory sent the extraction system just a few days ago, and that was the final part. However, an unfortunate series of events have also occurred. Dr. ███ █████ has died. The cause of death is currently unknown, but he died peacefully in his sleep. Coincidentally, my doppelganger, despite being overt regarding his existence, disappeared the day after Dr. ███ █████’s death. I can’t say whether there is any correlation between my doppelganger’s disappearance and Dr. ███ █████’s death. On the bright side, the D-Class personnel that were sent down from Station Tau have supported me since. Other smaller bases have been constructed around Occator-Alpha. It’s like an entire colony done here, and it will only become larger once we activate our machine, which we dubbed “Extractor-XXXX” and acquire SCP-XXXX. I am sure we can find its origin, and find its containment method. Activation begins tomorrow, and so will my next report. Wish us luck.</p>
<p><strong>LOG-008:</strong> [DATA EXPUNGED]</p>
